              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad and Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, altogether from Ibn Mahboub, from Abu Hamza Al-Thumali, from Abu Abdullah (عليه السلام), who said:",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 29,
            "word_start": 0
          },
          {
            "chunk_type": "opening",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "Rasool-Allah (صلى الله عليه وآله وسلم) said:",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 37,
            "word_start": 29
          },
          {
            "chunk_type": "body",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "Indeed, Allah took a covenant with the mu'min (believer) regarding four tribulations, the least (serious) of these being a mu'min who holds the same belief yet envies him; or a hypocrite who follows his tracks (to harm him); or a Satan who tempts him astray; or a disbeliever who witnesses his striving (against him). So what would remain of the mu'min after all of this?",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 67,
            "word_start": 37
          }
