        "seo_questions": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "What are the four tribulations Allah has covenanted every believer to endure, according to a hadith of Rasool-Allah (SAWW) in al-Kafi?",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
        "summaries": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "In this hadith, Imam al-Sadiq (عليه السلام) transmits the words of Rasool-Allah (صلى الله عليه وآله وسلم), revealing that Allah has taken a solemn covenant with every believer to endure four categories of tribulation: envy from a fellow believer who shares his creed, persecution by a hypocrite who trails him, temptation by Satan, and the open hostility of a disbeliever who opposes his striving in faith. The closing rhetorical question — 'So what would remain of the mu'min after this?' — is a profound expression of the relentless weight of trials the believer must bear, underscoring the centrality of patience (sabr) as a divine covenant and not merely a virtue.",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
